## Random IIT-JEE–level question

**Topic:** Electrostatics — capacitors and dielectrics

**Question:**  
A parallel-plate capacitor of capacitance \(C_0\) is charged and then disconnected from the battery. A dielectric of relative permittivity \(K\) is inserted so that it fills half the plate area and the full separation between the plates. Find:

1. The new capacitance \(C'\)
2. The ratio of final to initial electrostatic energy, \(U'/U_0\)

**Answer:**

\[
\boxed{C'=\frac{K+1}{2}C_0}
\]

Because the battery is disconnected, charge remains constant:

\[
\boxed{\frac{U'}{U_0}=\frac{2}{K+1}}
\]

---

## Knowledge graph

```mermaid
graph TD
    Q[Problem] -->|contains| CAP[Parallel-plate capacitor]
    CAP -->|initial capacitance| C0["C₀ = ε₀A/d"]

    Q -->|states| DISC[Battery disconnected]
    DISC -->|implies| CONS[Free charge Q is conserved]

    Q -->|introduces| DIEL[Dielectric]
    DIEL -->|relative permittivity| K[K]
    DIEL -->|occupies| HALF[Half of plate area]

    HALF -->|creates configuration| PAR[Two parallel capacitors]

    PAR -->|dielectric branch| CD["C_d = Kε₀(A/2)/d = KC₀/2"]
    PAR -->|vacuum branch| CV["C_v = ε₀(A/2)/d = C₀/2"]

    CD -->|contributes to| CEQ[Equivalent capacitance C′]
    CV -->|contributes to| CEQ
    PAR -->|uses rule| ADD[Capacitances add in parallel]
    ADD -->|derives| CEQ["C′ = C_d + C_v = (K+1)C₀/2"]

    CONS -->|selects energy formula| EN["U = Q²/(2C)"]
    CEQ -->|substituted into| RATIO["U′/U₀ = C₀/C′"]
    EN -->|derives| RATIO
    RATIO -->|equals| FINAL["2/(K+1)"]
```

---

## Knowledge-graph triples

| Subject | Relation | Object |
|---|---|---|
| Problem | involves | Parallel-plate capacitor |
| Capacitor | has initial capacitance | \(C_0=\varepsilon_0A/d\) |
| Battery | is | Disconnected |
| Battery disconnected | implies | Charge conservation |
| Dielectric | has relative permittivity | \(K\) |
| Dielectric | occupies | Half plate area |
| Half-area filling | produces | Parallel configuration |
| Dielectric region | has capacitance | \(KC_0/2\) |
| Vacuum region | has capacitance | \(C_0/2\) |
| Parallel configuration | uses | Capacitance addition |
| Equivalent capacitor | has capacitance | \((K+1)C_0/2\) |
| Charge conservation | selects | \(U=Q^2/(2C)\) |
| Energy formula | gives | \(U'/U_0=C_0/C'\) |
| Capacitance result | gives | \(U'/U_0=2/(K+1)\) |

### Answer-producing path

\[
\text{Half-area dielectric}
\rightarrow
\text{parallel capacitors}
\rightarrow
C_d+C_v
\rightarrow
C'=\frac{K+1}{2}C_0
\]

\[
\text{battery disconnected}
\rightarrow
Q=\text{constant}
\rightarrow
U=\frac{Q^2}{2C}
\rightarrow
\frac{U'}{U_0}=\frac{2}{K+1}
\]

