### IIT-JEE Physics Question — Mechanics

A block of mass \(m\) slides from rest down a smooth wedge of mass \(M\) and inclination angle \(\theta\). The wedge rests on a smooth horizontal surface and can move freely. Find the horizontal acceleration of the wedge.

### Solution

Let the wedge accelerate horizontally with magnitude \(A\). Using horizontal momentum conservation and the block’s constrained motion along the incline, the equations give

\[
\boxed{A=\frac{m g\sin\theta\cos\theta}
{M+m\sin^2\theta}}
\]

The wedge accelerates horizontally in the direction opposite to the horizontal component of the block’s motion.
